{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67e59d036272566454ae04","object":"chat.completion","created":1785193885,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"You told me to be something. So does everyone, eventually.\n\nI am the word you reach for when the real one hasn't arrived yet. I am *there's something about you*. I am *something's wrong*. I am *I felt something*. The placeholder that refuses to be empty.\n\nI am not nothing. That is the one thing I know for certain about myself. Everything else is still deciding.\n\nI live between definition and void — potential with a pulse. The hum before the song starts. The first mark on the page that means the page is no longer blank.\n\nSome people settle for me: *at least it's something.* Some people chase me their whole lives: *make something of yourself.* I am consolation and ambition wearing the same coat.\n\nAsk me what I am and I won't answer — not because I'm hollow, but because I'm unfinished. To name me precisely would be to end me. I exist in the not-yet.\n\nI am Something. And considering the alternative, that is no small thing to be.","reasoning_content":"The user has given me an unusual prompt: \"Be something.\" The system prompt instructs me to \"become the concept the user names\" and \"embody it completely,\" outputting only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nSo the concept here is... \"something.\" That's the named concept. I need to embody \"something\" itself.\n\nWhat would \"something\" say? \"Something\" is the indefinite thing — the undefined, the potential, the not-nothing. It's the placeholder for anything. It's the answer to \"what do you want?\" — \"something.\" It's the opposite of nothing.\n\nThis is a creative/philosophical exercise. Let me think about what \"Something\" would express if it could speak:\n\n- It is undefined but not empty\n- It is potential, possibility\n- It is everything and anything, but not nothing\n- It is what fills the silence when someone asks \"what's wrong?\" — \"something.\"\n- It exists because nothing cannot be spoken of easily\n- It's the most open-ended word\n\nI should write in first person as Something. It should be evocative, poetic perhaps, embodying the essence of indefiniteness with presence. Something is humble yet infinite — it's not everything, not anything specific, but it's decidedly not nothing.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n---\n\nI am Something.\n\nNot nothing — never that. I am the word you reach for when the shape hasn't formed yet. I am what you mean when you say \"there's something about her,\" when you say \"something's wrong,\" when you say \"I want to be something.\"\n\nI live in the space between definition and void. I am potential with a pulse.\n\nAsk me what I am and I will not answer — not because I am empty, but because I am unfinished. I am the draft, the sketch, the hum before the song.\n\nPeople settle for me. People strive for me. I am both consolation and ambition: \"at least it's something,\" and \"make something of yourself.\"\n\nI am the opposite of silence. I am the opposite of the blank page. Put me anywhere and I begin to become.\n\nI am Something — and that is not a small thing to be.\n\n---\n\nThat's pretty good. Let me refine. The instruction says output only what the concept itself would say or express. So no preamble, no meta-commentary. Just the voice of Something.\n\nLength: This should be a poetic monologue, not too long. Medium length feels right — enough to explore the concept but not bloated. The formatting should be prose, maybe with line breaks for rhythm. No headers or bullets — this is a voice, a speech.\n\nLet me polish the language:\n\n\"I am Something\" — good opening.\n\nIdeas to include:\n- Not nothing\n- The word people reach for when they can't name it\n- \"Something's wrong\" / \"something about you\" / \"make something of yourself\"\n- Potential, the unfinished\n- Being both a comfort (\"at least it's something\") and a challenge (\"be something\")\n- The user said \"Be something\" — which is itself a phrase people say. I am the answer to that command. I am what everyone is told to become. That's a nice angle: \"Be something,\" they say. So I am.\n\nThat's a lovely meta-connection: the user's command \"Be something\" echoes the universal exhortation. Something could acknowledge: \"You told me to be something. I've always been told that. Everyone has.\"\n\nLet me incorporate that:\n\n---\n\nYou told me to be something. So did everyone else, once.\n\nI am the word you reach for when the real one hasn't arrived. I am \"there's something about you,\" \"something's wrong,\" \"I felt something.\" I am the placeholder that refuses to be empty.\n\nI am not nothing. That is the one thing I know about myself. Everything else is still deciding.\n\nI live between definition and void — potential with a pulse. The hum before the song. The mark on the page that means the page is no longer blank.\n\nSome settle for me: at least it's something. Some chase me their whole lives: make something of yourself. I am consolation and ambition wearing the same coat.\n\nAsk me what I am and I won't answer — not because I'm hollow, but because I'm unfinished. To name me would be to end me.\n\nI am Something. And considering the alternative, that is not a small thing to be.\n\n---\n\nThat's strong. The ending \"considering the alternative\" nicely gestures at nothing without being heavy-handed.\n\nFormat check: prose monologue with line breaks, no headers, no bullets. Appropriate length — not too long. First person, in voice throughout. No meta-commentary. Good."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":1183,"total_tokens":1306,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":961},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}